<title>UK: Bankers Trust $100 million 10-year step-up FRN. [CORRECTED 11:26 GMT]</title>
<headline>Bankers Trust $100 million 10-year step-up FRN. [CORRECTED 11:26 GMT]</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-07-09</dateline>
<text>
<p>The following floating-rate issue</p>
<p>was announced by lead manager Bear Stearns.</p>
<p> BORROWER   BANKERS TRUST INTERNATIONAL PLC</p>
<p> AMT    $100 MLN	BASE	 3M-LIBOR  MATURITY  * 18.JUL.07</p>
<p> TYPE	 FRN	 MARGIN   * +25 BP    PAY DATE  L 17.JUL.97</p>
<p> LAST MOODY A2	  ISS PRICE  99.773    FULL FEES   0.25</p>
<p> LAST S&amp;P   A	   REOFFER    99.773</p>
<p> NOTES   *  CALLABLE AFTER FIVE (corrects from first) YEAR,  COUPON STEPS UP TO 3MLIBOR</p>
<p>		PLUS 75 BP AFTER FIVE YEARS.</p>
<p>	   L  LONG FIRST COUPON</p>
<p> LISTING    LUX	 DENOMS (K) 10-100    SALE LIMITS US/UK</p>
<p> NEG PLG    NO	  CRS DEFLT  NO	  FORCE MAJ   YES</p>
<p> GOV LAW    NEW YORK  HOME CTRY  U.S.	TAX PROVS   =</p>
<p> MGT/UND    0.125     SELL CONC  0.125     PRAECIPUUM  =</p>
<p> NOTES	ISSUED OFF EMTN PROGRAMME</p>
<p>-- London Newsroom +44 171 542 8863</p>
</text>
